OL,3,GNEWSAConcerns after bluetongue case
OL,4,Aidentified in Norfolk
OL,5,
OL,6,FConcerns have been raised following the
OL,7,Ffirst case of bluetongue virus
OL,8,Fconfirmed in eastern England this year.
OL,10,FThe Department for Environment, Food &
OL,11,FRural Affairs (Defra) said an incidence
OL,12,Fof the disease, which is caused by
OL,13,Fbiting midges, was recorded near King's
OL,14,FLynn in Norfolk on 24 August.
OL,16,FSo far in the UK in the 2026-27
OL,17,Fbluetongue reporting season, 825 cases
OL,18,Fhave been identified in a number of
OL,19,Fsheep, cattle and alpacas, and one
OL,20,Fllama.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
